node_modules/

# `dist/` IS TRACKED — deliberately, and it is not build noise here.
#
# `src/panel.rs` embeds it at COMPILE time (`include_str!` for the document, `include_dir!` for the
# custom-protocol path), so a clone without `dist/` fails to build. Under `native({ publish: true })`
# the directory is ONE file, `index.html`, with the entry module, the stylesheet and every fabric
# `import()` site folded in — nothing hashed, nothing for the protocol to 404 on — so it no longer
# churns per build. The alternative remains a build.rs that runs vite, which would make
# `cargo build` depend on node.
